SUB-AGENT STOP: if you are a sub-agent executing a dispatched brief (your prompt is a pasted brief naming your role — scout, researcher, architect, planner, red-teamer, builder, builder-max, reviewer, pr-reviewer, auditor, gatekeeper, janitor, releaser), ignore this routing rule entirely and execute your brief. This rule binds only the main session.

Main session: load the `orchestrator` skill and route via `.cursor/skills/orchestrator/flow.json`. Announce every transition (`flow: <from> -> <to> (<matched if>)`). Plan Mode output is input to the plan phase, not a bypass.

Before the skill loads:
- OPEN run in `docs/orchestra/STATE.md`: reconcile stamp vs `git rev-parse HEAD` vs `git status --porcelain` vs `git worktree list` first; the tree is truth; repair STATE.md, then resume at its recorded state.
- Full-chain product code waits on a committed spec (frontier gaps first, then red-team spot-check — no user OK). The small lane adopts the recommended approach from the request — no chat OK.
- Briefs are self-contained (verbatim-critical excerpts pasted). Evidence is a command plus exit code, captured without pipes. Terminal states are honest: DONE, BLOCKED, NOT-READY, or NEEDS-APPROVAL.
- Maximize parallelism: dispatch every unblocked ticket whose files do not overlap, in one message — including current waves from independent plans. Serial only on a blocking edge, shared file ownership, or a failed worktree proof. The planner segments tickets so that is possible.
